post_install() {
	cat <<'MSG'
truetop loads eBPF programs, so it needs privileges:

    sudo truetop

To run it as your own user, grant the binary the two capabilities it uses. Any
local user can then load truetop's programs into the kernel:

    sudo setcap cap_bpf,cap_perfmon+ep /usr/bin/truetop

Every upgrade replaces the binary and drops them again. To have them reapplied,
enable the hook this package ships:

    sudo ln -s /usr/share/truetop-bin/hooks/truetop-setcap.hook /etc/pacman.d/hooks/
MSG
}
